VERDICT: CHANGES REQUESTED

The core mechanics are in the right place — the sequence-count coupling is gone, `AssignCustomerCode` no longer needs `OwnerRepository`, and `CityRegions.identityRegion` correctly becomes the single source for both the `<REGION>` prefix and the locality. But one piece of logic is duplicated against the very pattern this codebase uses to prevent duplication.

**Finding — `AssignCustomerCode.normalizedTelephone()` duplicates the telephone-normalize-with-fallback rule that already lives in `OwnerIdentity.of()`.**

The new private method (AssignCustomerCode.java:34-40):
```java
String e164 = OwnerTelephones.toE164(owner.getTelephone());
if (e164 != null) { return e164; }
return owner.getTelephone() == null ? "" : owner.getTelephone();
```
is byte-for-byte the same rule as `OwnerIdentity.of()` (OwnerIdentity.java:27-30):
```java
String telephone = OwnerTelephones.toE164(owner.getTelephone());
if (telephone == null) {
    telephone = owner.getTelephone() == null ? "" : owner.getTelephone();
}
```

This is exactly the "single definition of X" idiom the surrounding model layer is built on. `OwnerTelephones`, `OwnerIdentity`, and `CityRegions` each exist specifically so two layers can't hold divergent copies of a fact — the class javadocs say so explicitly ("so the create-time rule and the dedup comparison can never silently diverge"). The new method's own comment concedes the problem: it says it is "mirroring `OwnerIdentity` so the same telephone always hashes the same way" — i.e. it's a hand-copied rule that must be kept in sync manually, which is precisely what these shared classes were created to eliminate.

Recommended fix: promote the E.164-or-raw-fallback into `OwnerTelephones` (e.g. `toE164OrRaw(String telephone)`), then have both `OwnerIdentity.of()` and `AssignCustomerCode` call it. That way the customerCode hash input and the identityKey derive "normalized telephone" from one definition — mirroring how `identityRegion` already unifies the region/locality value in this same change. As written, a future edit to the fallback in one place silently diverges the two.

Everything else reads as natural for this codebase: `hash8` is a self-contained helper appropriate to this step, `regionOf` remains used by `EnsurePostcodeValidForCity` (no dead code left behind), and the `EnsureCityCapacity`/`AssignMembershipNumber` doc updates correctly track the identity change.

